\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Massless laws and their constraints}
\date{2026-10-30}

\p{For the [alternating four-cycle](fdip-0003) with weights
#{(1,t,1,t)}, #{t>0}, the zero-mass action has an infinite full-space
integral. On the [mean-zero field space](fdip-0031)
#{H=\{\phi:\sum_v\phi(v)=0\}}, its induced three-dimensional volume
instead gives the [constrained normalizer](fdip-000C)
##{Z_H=\frac{(2\pi)^{3/2}}{\sqrt{8t(1+t)}}.}
At #{t=1}, the resulting law has
#{\operatorname{Var}(\phi(0)-\phi(2))=1}, as the
[zero-mass cycle calculation](fdip-0038) shows.}

\p{The [positive Gaussian law](fdip-0017) on the orthogonal complement
of the kernel yields this constrained probability and its
[pseudoinverse covariance](fdip-0032). [Kernel factorization](fdip-0033)
and [projected limits](fdip-0034) distinguish the divergent full
normalizer from finite difference observables. [Pinning a vertex](fdip-0035)
gives another constraint, with a generally different coordinate
covariance; the [two-vertex comparison](fdip-0036) makes the distinction explicit.}

\transclude{fdip-0031}
